===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[do]] (something); to [[execute]].
#: {{ux|en|The scientists '''performed''' several experiments.}}
#: {{ux|en|It took him only twenty minutes to '''perform''' the task.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To exhibit an expected pattern of behavior; to function; to work.
#: {{ux|en|The new employee '''performs''' well.}}
## {{lb|en|sexology|uncommon}} Of a man, to be able to [[initiate]] or [[fulfill]] an [[act]] of [[sexual intercourse]].
# {{lb|en|law}} To act in a way set forth in a contract.
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To act in accordance with (a contract); to fulfill one’s terms of (a contract).
##: {{ux|en|Failure to '''perform''' a contract on time may constitute a [[breach of contract]].}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To fulfill contractually agreed-to terms.
##: {{ux|en|They entered into an agreement and now they are obliged to '''perform'''.}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To do (something) in front of an audience, such as acting or music, often in order to entertain.
#: {{ux|en|She will '''perform''' in the play.}}
#: {{ux|en|The magician '''performed''' badly—none of his tricks worked.}}
#: {{ux|en|The string quartet '''performed''' three pieces by Haydn.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Coriolanus|III|ii|passage='''Perform''' a part thou hast not done before.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension|transitive}} To behave theatrically so as to give the impression of (a quality, character trait, etc.); to feign.
#: {{ux|en|The accused only '''performed''' remorse.}}
